// @run
// @log 200
// @hint redundant type annotation: `b` is inferred as `B` — remove it to lean on inference
// CLOSED — this was `xfail-false-reject-call-result-union-binding.vl`, and the prefix is
// dropped per this directory's README ("when it closes, drop the prefix and flip the file to
// @run + @log"). A declared struct produced by a CALL, bound to an INLINE union-annotated
// const. Sound program, refused with `emitProgram: ref valtype with no interned shape`.
//
// THE OLD HEADER'S DIAGNOSIS WAS RIGHT AND ITS TRIGGER WAS WRONG. It named the SAME-SHAPE
// COLLAPSE — `A` and `B` here have identical fields, the annotation route dedups its members
// with `sameVariantTy`, and the inline `A | B` keeps ONE member — and it named the consequence
// (`registerInlineUnion` pushes BOTH names into `uVariants` anyway, so `collectS` refuses both
// a standalone struct row). What it never was is a CALL-RESULT-IN-A-UNION-POSITION defect.
// Measured one axis at a time, the collapse alone is the trigger and the union position is not
// involved at all — this program has the identical reject with the call result never touching
// the union:
//
//     type A = { v: i32 }
//     type B = { v: i32 }
//     function mkB(): B { return { v: 200 } }
//     const b: A | B = { v: 1 }     // the collapsed union, initialized by a LITERAL
//     print(mkB().v)                // `B` in a signature is what has no valtype
//
// Any function signature mentioning `A` or `B` does it — a param (`function f(x: B)`) as
// readily as a return. Drop the `A | B` binding and it compiles; give `A` and `B` DISTINCT
// field sets and it compiles; write the union as a declared alias (`type U = A | B`) and it
// compiles. Only the inline spelling of a collapsing pair fails, and it fails at the FIRST
// position that needs `B`'s valtype, which is why the old bisect landed on the call.
//
// THE FIX IS #1803's, ONE EARLY RETURN FURTHER IN. That change taught the ANNOTATION route to
// feed `cVariantMemberTyIxs` (`annRegisterVariantMembers`) so the checker and `collectU` agree
// about which declared structs are variant members — but `annUnionInnerTy` returns its single
// member before reaching that call, so a union that DEDUPS to one member never registered.
// `annUnionPushDistinctMember` (typecheck) now registers the pair at the moment the dedup drops
// one, which is the only place the pre-dedup arity is still in hand. The DECLARED spelling is
// the control and always worked for exactly this reason: pass 0b's `UnionDecl` arm does not
// dedup, so its `members.length >= 2` gate passes and the shared index registers.
//
// A | A IS NOT THIS, and the gate says so: the registration fires only when the two members are
// DISTINCT arena entries that are mutually assignable. The same entry twice is a degenerate
// repeat the emitter also collapses (one distinct NAME, no variant rows, `collectS` keeps the
// struct row), and registering it moved `const b: A | A = mkA()` from RUN-OK to this very
// reject — measured, and the reason the gate is not just `sameVariantTy`.
//
// THE B184 DEAD END IS NOT REVISITED. Flipping only the emitter's KIND made 7 of 10 repros
// compile into INVALID MODULES ("the signature now says variant while the body still BUILDS
// the plain struct"); registering the member moves the producer too, so the value IS the
// variant. `types/variant-as-value.vl` — which B185 found in conflict with minting a struct
// row — is untouched: no struct row is minted for `A` or `B` anywhere.
//
// THE NULLABLE RESIDUE IS UNMOVED, BY DESIGN. Add `const n: B | null = null` beside the
// binding and this program is refused exactly as it is on master:
// `annCommitVariantMembers` excludes any arm the module also uses as `T | null`, because the
// niche rep and the variant rep are incompatible and calling such a struct a variant turns a
// loud reject into check-clean INVALID WASM (that exclusion's own 24-cell measurement). The
// family stays filed at `unions/error-nullable-variant-unsupported.vl`.
//
// STILL OPEN, and NOT this family: a field read directly off a union-returning CALL,
// `function g(): A | B { … }` then `g().v`, is `emitProgram: field access but no struct type
// declared`. It is the same on master, it is the same for the DECLARED alias `type U = A | B`,
// and it is the same for a DISTINCT-shape pair — so it is a union-call-receiver gap, not a
// same-shape one. Binding the call first (`const r = g()`) runs.
type A = { tag: i32, v: i32 }
type B = { tag: i32, v: i32 }
function mkB(): B { return { tag: 2, v: 200 } }
const b: A | B = mkB()
print(b.v)
